From: BananaOS Duo Lite bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] drm/msm/dp: discover fixed sink before selecting mode bpp

The hardwired WL818S is powered by downstream bridge pre_enable callbacks.
Read its capabilities in the DP pre_enable callback before set_mode uses
them. Previously prepare_link did this in atomic_enable, after set_mode
clamped bpp against an all-zero link_info. The first boot selected 18 bpp,
whereas resume reused the discovered 270000 kHz / one-lane link and chose
24 bpp. Preserve the existing eDP path and runtime-PM reference pairing.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/msm/dp/dp_display.c
@@ -642,7 +642,7 @@
 
 	drm_dbg_dp(dp->drm_dev, "sink_count=%d\n", dp->link->sink_count);
 
-	if (msm_dp_display->is_edp || msm_dp_display_fixed_sink(dp))
+	if (msm_dp_display->is_edp)
 		msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
 
 	rc = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(&msm_dp_display->pdev->dev);
@@ -1437,6 +1437,20 @@
 		return;
 	crtc_state = drm_atomic_get_new_crtc_state(state, crtc);
 
+	/* Downstream pre_enable has powered the fixed sink. Discover its link
+	 * before mode bpp is bounded by link_info; on the first modeset that
+	 * structure is still empty. Keep the HPD runtime-PM get paired with
+	 * post_disable, exactly as when it ran from prepare_link.
+	 */
+	if (msm_dp_display_fixed_sink(dp)) {
+		int ret = msm_dp_hpd_plug_handle(dp);
+
+		if (ret) {
+			DRM_ERROR("fixed sink discovery failed, rc=%d\n", ret);
+			return;
+		}
+	}
+
 	/*
 	 * The DPU encoder's .atomic_enable() reads the mode's YUV420 / wide bus
 	 * state and runs before the bridge's .atomic_enable(), so the mode must
